  "details": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to delete department permission bindings via the DELETE /sys/sysDepartPermission/deleteBatch endpoint. Attackers can obtain row ids from the unguarded list endpoint and submit them in the ids parameter to remove menus and buttons departments can grant to their roles.",
